@title INC-3017: listing photo upload outage
@subtitle Stonebridge Realty, Listings Platform team, 2026-08-27. Blameless postmortem.
kpi Duration | 112 minutes | from 10:15 UTC | bad
kpi Peak upload failures | 100% | at peak | bad
kpi Listings with missing photos | 8,340 | left behind | bad
kpi Support tickets | 412 | during the outage | neutral

## Summary
A storage policy change meant to restrict bucket access to our VPC endpoint also blocked uploads made with pre-signed URLs from agents' phones. Every mobile upload returned 403. The outage lasted 112 minutes.

## Timeline (UTC)
- **10:15** Policy change applied through Terraform.
- **10:22** Uploads begin failing with 403. This is the first symptom.
- **10:31** First customer ticket reaches support.
- **10:48** Incident declared Sev2.
- **11:20** The policy diff is identified as the cause. This is the turning point.
- **11:58** Hotfix applied, removing the deny statement.
- **12:07** Uploads recover.

## Why it was not caught
- The change was tested only from the office network.
- Staging has no mobile upload test.
- The policy linter does not model pre-signed URLs.

## What went well
- The declared incident had a clear commander within 17 minutes.
- The rollback took under 10 minutes once the cause was known.

## Action items
- **Add a pre-signed URL upload test to staging.** Greta Lindqvist, due 2026-09-18.
- **Require policy changes to be applied to staging first.** Omar Haddad, due 2026-09-25.
- **Alert when upload 403s exceed 2 percent for 5 minutes.** Listings on-call, due 2026-09-11.
